title: Another Gospel – False Doctrine Answered
description: False doctrine: one gospel and works gospels accursed, Rome's false gospel, idols and icons, Calvinism, original sin, dispensationalism and its teachers, charismatic false gifts, false prophets of peace, Mystery Babylon, and the harrowing of hell, from the teachings on false doctrine.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-false.html
highlight: false; gospel

# One deck for the doctrine "False doctrine" (314 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.
# At the author's word: false teachers are named and points kept sharp; a crude word is replaced, not the point
# ("autistically literal" -> "woodenly literal").

=== Introduction
--- Another Gospel [title]
overline: Doctrine · False doctrine
heading: Another Gospel
sub: False gospels, false prophets and false churches.
refs: Galatians 1:6-9; 2 Peter 2:1; Matthew 7:15-16; 1 John 4:1; 2 Corinthians 11:3-4
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 16364, 10381, 4395
--- Let him be accursed
big: Galatians 1:8 | mark: let him be accursed
p: The one criteria the Bible gives for identifying a false believer or false teacher is do they add works to the gospel. Not behavior after being saved. Not by how good they are. Not what church they go to, or any other thing, but what they trusted in.
p: Paul is writing churches he founded on the gospel, the only good news that we are forgiven all sin and given eternal life through Jesus Christ, because Jews came behind him, telling the Gentile believers they must add the law.
read: app:doctrine-false~16364 | The one test of a false teacher

=== Works gospels accursed
# from 14034, 11401, 11412
--- Lordship salvation
kicker: Works gospels
big: Acts 16:30-31 | mark: Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved
p: Lordship salvation is a false doctrine, put forth by vipers that say you have to “make Jesus the Lord of your life” in order to be saved. That you have to “repent of your sins” or you cannot be saved. Imagine a seeking person asking “Sirs, what must I do to be saved?” and the answer is “well, you have to repent of your sins.”
p: Every religion that teaches eternal life is not a gift, that salvation is a “process,” would condemn each other in a circular firing squad yelling “HERETIC!” But they all agree with a false gospel of works.

# from 4902, 12043, 4472, 4436, 11183
--- Judaizers: Satan's main play
kicker: Works gospels
big: Galatians 5:1 | mark: be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage
p: Paul warns again and again of the Judaizers, demanding a return to Hebrew roots, the law, the carnal ordinances, circumcision of the flesh. It is told to us over and over because it is Satan's main play against us. Giant red flags.
p: Not eating meat on Fridays, and more and more in Judaized evangelical circles, the Levitical dietary laws: *commanding to abstain from meats... doctrines of devils* ([[1 Timothy 4:1-3]]).

# from 13157, 10825, 11403, 10745, 5738
--- The fruit of works religion
kicker: Works gospels
big: Romans 10:3 | mark: going about to establish their own righteousness
p: Churches that teach repentance of sin as a condition of salvation tend to be the least forgiving. They take pride in their own righteousness, and compare themselves to the sins of others. Works-based false religion is about pride. It is the root of every false religion, and a form of control over a fearful population.
p: “Perseverance of the saints”: if you backslide, you never really were saved. A backwards, works-based “lose your salvation” heresy.
read: app:doctrine-false~11401 | Lordship salvation is a false gospel
read: app:doctrine-false~4902 | Judaizers: Satan's main play
read: app:doctrine-false~13157 | Repent of sins teachers are least forgiving

=== Rome's false gospel
# from 14756, 5202, 9251, 13936, 13944
--- Trent's anathema
kicker: Rome's false gospel
quote: If any one saith, that by faith alone the impious is justified... let him be anathema. | Council of Trent, Canon IX
p: Catholicism is leading people straight to Hell with a false gospel. There is no such thing as purgatory, invented in the 12th century. Indulgences monetized prayers for the dead. Penance is a slap in the face to the finished work of Jesus Christ. If you think you have to work off the debt of sin, it isn't forgiven ([[Galatians 2:21]]).

# from 5265, 5268, 2382, 15610
--- Upon this rock
kicker: Rome's false gospel
big: Matthew 16:23 | mark: Get thee behind me, Satan
p: Matthew 16 contains the one half-sentence, stripped of all context, that Catholics use to justify the false church's existence. Just a few verses later, Peter, their “first pope,” is rebuked by Jesus as Satan.
p: The Catholic church is not a rock, it's not even a stone like Peter; it is shifting, ever-changing. Sacerdotalism: a priest class as mediators. But we have one High Priest, and every believer a priest ([[1 Peter 2:9]]).

# from 12165, 12166, 4967, 14802, 6120, 17524
--- The queen of heaven
kicker: Rome's false gospel
big: Jeremiah 44:17 | mark: to burn incense unto the queen of heaven
p: Mary as “co-redeemer” and “co-mediatrix,” distributing from a “Treasury of Merit.” There's very little difference between this and the Jews in Egypt worshipping the queen of heaven. The idea that Mary was sinless would mean she was not in need of His grace ([[Luke 1:47]]).
p: Mary was saved by faith alone. Her perpetual virginity is extra-biblical nonsense: Jesus had half-brothers and sisters ([[Mark 6:3]]).

# from 1558, 10151, 11359, 17721, 13712
--- Not a wafer
kicker: Rome's false gospel
big: John 6:63 | mark: the words that I speak unto you, they are spirit, and they are life
p: Peter understood: Jesus has the words of eternal life. Not His literal flesh and blood to consume, but the words that by faith grant eternal life ([[John 6:68]]). The command not to consume blood extends to the New Testament ([[Acts 15:29]]).
p: *Their drink offerings of blood will I not offer* ([[Psalms 16:4]]). The mass refuted.

# from 7075, 13950, 5813
--- The whore and her daughters
kicker: Rome's false gospel
big: Revelation 17:5 | mark: MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS
p: The whore of Babylon, the Roman Catholic Church and its Protestant harlot daughters deny the liberty that is in Christ, so that its adherents stay yoked to trying to justify themselves. When Great Tribulation comes, it will be Catholics under the whore mother church doing the beheading.
p: Do I hate Catholics? It is the organization and its false pagan doctrines that I hate. As for Catholics, I love them and would that they repent and believe the Gospel ([[Romans 10:1]]).
read: app:doctrine-false~14756 | Catholicism and the false gospel
read: app:doctrine-false~12165 | The queen of heaven and Mary worship
read: app:doctrine-false~5813 | Do I hate Catholics?

=== Idols and icons condemned
# from 10206, 7083, 12910, 17758, 15390
--- Rome edited the second commandment
kicker: Idols and icons
big: Exodus 20:4-5 | mark: Thou shalt not bow down thyself to them, nor serve them
p: A Catholic “Pope” ordered the 2nd commandment edited so they could use idols, and split the 10th in two to still have 10. Those kneeling before idols are worshiping. Those lighting a candle in front of them are serving. When a Catholic tells you you don't understand what “worship” means, they are changing the meaning of the word.

# from 12638, 14687, 14652, 7082, 14994
--- Nehushtan, relics and the rosary
kicker: Idols and icons
big: 2 Kings 18:4 | mark: and he called it Nehushtan
p: The brazen serpent is cited by Catholics and Orthodox to justify idolatry. To a man, those who brought it up had never heard of Nehushtan. Elisha's bones are used to justify the veneration of relics ([[2 Kings 13:21]]).
p: The rosary is pagan vain repetition, ten prayers to Mary for every one to God ([[Matthew 6:7]]). Praying to saints to find lost items is an incantation, treating them as house gods.

# from 13742, 13919, 14016
--- Micah's house of gods
kicker: Idols and icons
big: Judges 17:6 | mark: every man did that which was right in his own eyes
p: Micah established his own church full of idols, and hired a young Levite to be his house priest, calling him “father.” Dagon fell before the ark, a useless idol ([[1 Samuel 5:4]]).
p: People in false religion dress it up as Saul did: buildings made of marble and images laid with gold. *To obey is better than sacrifice* ([[1 Samuel 15:22]]).
read: app:doctrine-false~7083 | Rome edited the second commandment
read: app:doctrine-false~12638 | Nehushtan: no license for idolatry

=== Calvinism refuted
# from 13992, 1273, 15556, 17119
--- For God so loved the world
kicker: Calvinism refuted
big: John 1:9 | mark: lighteth every man that cometh into the world
p: If you believe in “Limited Atonement,” you don't believe the Gospel ([[John 3:16]]). (RIP limited atonement.) If God “chooses” someone for His own purpose, that introduces merit. They make grace no more grace ([[Romans 11:6]]).
p: Their “unconditional election” assumes they are selected because of a personal quality they possess. They say things like this in pride, trying to sound humble.

# from 239, 4580, 10838, 252, 17176
--- Who first trusted in Christ
kicker: Calvinism refuted
big: Ephesians 1:12-13 | mark: who first trusted in Christ; after that ye believed
p: The strongest case for special boyism undone with one conditional phrase. What is predestined? The saved, or Christ Jesus by whom we are saved? “Sovereign” reduces God to a puppet master micromanaging all of reality.
p: Free will isn't the argument against Calvinism. Responsibility is. The entire testimony, from the garden onward, is about informed choice ([[Deuteronomy 30:19]]).
read: app:doctrine-false~239 | Who first trusted in Christ
read: app:doctrine-false~15556 | Calvinism makes grace no more grace

=== Original sin refuted
# from 13696, 18013, 15976, 17149, 14637
--- We do not inherit sin
kicker: Original sin refuted
big: Ezekiel 18:20 | mark: The son shall not bear the iniquity of the father
p: We do not inherit sin. Babies go to Heaven ([[2 Samuel 12:23]]). The idea that babies are born guilty was created to keep people going to the Roman Catholic apostate Church.
p: Original sin immediately stirs the mother to ask “What about my baby?” As soon as you are water baptizing babies, you've put faith in a rite and a priest and a church. Not Jesus. Paedobaptism is accursed, being another gospel.
read: app:doctrine-false~13696 | We do not inherit sin

=== Dispensationalism and its teachers
# from 11606, 11607, 13426, 13423, 16228
--- Scofield, Bullinger, Ruckman
kicker: Dispensationalism
big: 1 Corinthians 15:11 | mark: so we preach, and so ye believed
p: The wicked Scofield study Bible took scripture and turned it on its head to embrace Zionism and dispensationalism, the foot in the door to Bible colleges and KJVO churches. Bullinger and O'Hair's “Grace Movement” teaches multiple gospels. One gospel: all are 1 Corinthians 15 Christians.
p: Ruckman taught another gospel. Serpent seed, the gap theory, UFOs and new Adams on alien planets, the kingdom given to unbelieving Jews saved by works. I don't care if you think he was right about the KJV.
read: app:doctrine-false~11606 | The Scofield Bible's heresies
read: app:doctrine-false~13426 | Bullingerism, a false gospel

=== Charismatic false gifts
# from 12827, 12828, 3877, 12821, 11159
--- Tongues were languages
kicker: Charismatic false gifts
big: Acts 2:6 | mark: every man heard them speak in his own language
p: The gift of tongues was known languages, for spreading the Gospel to the ends of the earth. Not babbling and shouting, flopping on the floor like a fish. Of all the spiritual gifts, it's the easiest to fake. Pride and wanting to seem more spiritual feeds the Pentecostal movement.
p: Faith healers are reprobate. Nadab and Abihu offered strange fire: the first thing the newly anointed priests did was add their own works ([[Leviticus 10:1-2]]).
read: app:doctrine-false~12828 | Pentecostal tongues are faked babbling
read: app:doctrine-false~12821 | Faith healers are reprobate

=== False prophets of peace
# from 11963, 14758, 16169, 12153, 11854
--- Peace, peace
kicker: False prophets
big: Jeremiah 6:14 | mark: saying, Peace, peace; when there is no peace
p: We can tell the false prophets by their preaching pleasant things easy on the ears. That “God is love” and He doesn't judge you, continue in your sin. The megachurches and television ministries preach prosperity and health to people with itching ears ([[2 Timothy 4:3]]).
p: Filthy dreamers that claim God has revealed some hidden truth to them ([[Jude 1:8]]). Untempered mortar ([[Ezekiel 13:10]]).

# from 5030, 17382, 9678, 6655, 18014
--- By their fruits
kicker: False prophets
big: Matthew 7:16 | mark: Ye shall know them by their fruits
p: Ecumenical people say we should accept all churches that call themselves “Christian.” But denominations of men that bring a false gospel of works are as wicked as the atheists and the Jews, even more. Chanting “Christ is King” and trusting in works isn't being led to Christ. It's being led to perdition.
p: Many Christians fall into the trap of being harmless as doves, while failing to be wise as serpents ([[Matthew 10:16]]).
read: app:doctrine-false~11963 | Peace, peace, when there is no peace
read: app:doctrine-false~9678 | False gospels of works and salvation by faith, not identity

=== Mystery Babylon
# from 8244, 8246, 8247, 16684, 12573
--- The whore and the bride
kicker: Mystery Babylon
big: Revelation 17:6 | mark: drunken with the blood of the saints
p: God speaks against idolatry as fornication, whoredoms. The whore represents the false church; the saved are the Lamb's wife, a bride ([[Revelation 21:9]]).
p: The Samaritans offered an ecumenical union to build the Lord's house, like Catholics seeking to join with a New Testament Baptist church. Zerubbabel rejected their offer, and persecution followed ([[Ezra 4:3]]). Korah's company: the first ecumenical council ([[Numbers 16:3]]).

=== The harrowing of hell refuted
# from 9823, 10313, 17324, 1435
--- He led captivity captive
kicker: The harrowing of hell
big: Ephesians 4:8 | mark: he led captivity captive
p: The “Harrowing of Hell” is a Catholic fable from the false “Gospel of Nicodemus,” that Jesus didn't go to Hell 3 days and 3 nights as the burnt sin offering. Ephesians 4 doesn't say Jesus freed saints from some holding room in Hell. It doesn't even hint at it.
p: Like all bad doctrine, it requires a woodenly literal interpretation of isolated verses, or doctrine built on a parable alone, as foolish as Nicodemus saying we'd have to crawl back inside our mother to be born again ([[John 3:4-7]]).
read: app:doctrine-false~9823 | The Harrowing of Hell is a Catholic fable

=== Abide in the doctrine of Christ
--- Abide in the Doctrine [title]
overline: False doctrine
heading: Abide in the Doctrine
big: 2 John 1:9 | mark: He that abideth in the doctrine of Christ, he hath both the Father and the Son
center: Grace is the unearned gift. Be satisfied with nothing less than the one gospel: believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved.
read: topic-israel | The Israel of God – Israel, the Church and Zionism
read: topic-reprobate | The Reprobate Mind – Given Over of God
